evelopmental disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/23150 {source=\"OMIM:621456\"} ! UNC13A\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0980947\nname: neurodevelopmental disorder with spasticity, thin corpus callosum, and decreased brain white matter\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:621460\"}\nxref: OMIM:621460 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"OMIM:621460\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/10439 {source=\"OMIM:621460\"} ! RPS6KC1\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0980965\nname: neurodevelopmental disorder with congenital cardiac defects and variable renal and ocular abnormalities\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:621474\"}\nxref: OMIM:621474 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"OMIM:621474\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/13610 {source=\"OMIM:621474\"} ! KDM2B\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0980968\nname: neurodevelopmental disorder with seizures, hypotonia, and variable spasticity\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:621482\"}\nxref: OMIM:621482 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"OMIM:621482\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/19405 {source=\"OMIM:621482\"} ! PGBD5\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0980990\nname: neurodevelopmental disorder with parkinsonism or other movement abnormalities\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0051076\"}\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:621506\"}\nxref: DOID:0051076 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: OMIM:621506 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"OMIM:621506\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0981032\nname: neurodevelopmental disorder with seizures and impaired intellectual and language development\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0051071\"}\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:621533\"}\nxref: DOID:0051071 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: OMIM:621533 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0981163\nname: Ebstein-Bezieau neurodevelopmental syndrome\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:621539\"}\nxref: OMIM:621539 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0981165\nname: Luo-Agrawal neurodevelopmental syndrome\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:621552\"}\nxref: OMIM:621552 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1010145\nname: PIP5K1C-related neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"Any neurodevelopmental disorder in which the cause of the disease is a monoallelic gain-of-function variation in the PIP5K1C gene leading to increased levels of phosphatidylinositol 4,5 bisphosphate. This disorder is characterized by intellectual disability, motor and speech delay, microcephaly, seizures, visual and ocular abnormalities, and craniofacial dysmorphic features.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/, PMID:37451268]\ncomment: This is a distinct entity from MONDO:0012656 lethal congenital contractural syndrome 3.\nsynonym: \"PIP5K1C-related neurodevelopmental disorder\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700092 ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/8996 ! PIP5K1C\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/8996 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/\"} ! PIP5K1C\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8931\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1040003\nname: KCND2-related neurodevelopmental disorder with or without seizures\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the KCND2 gene. This disorder is characterized by early-onset global developmental delay with impaired motor, speech and cognitive development. Patients often present muscle hypotonia, and less frequently, developmental epileptic encephalopathy, visual impairment and physical dysmorphisms.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, PMID:34245260]\nis_a: MONDO:0100500 {source=\"PMID:34245260\"} ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700092 ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/6238 ! KCND2\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8155\" xsd:string\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8489\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1040005\nname: PRPF19-related neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"Any neurodevelopmental disorder in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the PRPF19 gene. This disorder is characterised by developmental, motor and speech delay, and facial dysmorphisms. Most patients present mild to moderate intellectual disability, autism spectrum disorder or autistic features, and hypotonia. Other phenotypes observed less frequently include seizures, and visual and cardiac abnormalities.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, PMID:37962958]\nis_a: MONDO:0100500 {source=\"PMID:37962958\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\"} ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0100500 ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/17896 ! PRPF19\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8156\" xsd:string\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8489\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1040006\nname: CTR9-related neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"Any neurodevelopmental disorder in which the cause of the disease is a variation in the CTR9 gene. This disorder is characterised by varying degrees of intellectual disability, neurodevelopmental delay, hypotonia, fatigability, behavioral abnormalities including autism spectrum disorder, anxiety and aggressive behavior, cardiac anomalies, and mild facial dysmorphism.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, PMID:35468861, PMID:35499524, PMID:35717577]\nis_a: MONDO:0100500 {source=\"PMID:35468861\", source=\"PMID:35499524\", source=\"PMID:35717577\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862\"} ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0100500 ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/16850 ! CTR9\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8157\" xsd:string\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8489\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1040008\nname: CAMK2D-related neurodevelopmental disorder and dilated cardiomyopathy\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the CAMK2D gene. This disorder is characterised by intellectual disability, speech and motor delay, behavioural problems and dilated cardiomyopathy. Patients often present brain structural anomalies and hypotonia, and less frequently, seizures.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, PMID:37372357, PMID:38272033]\nis_a: MONDO:0100500 {source=\"PMID:37372357\", source=\"PMID:38272033\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\"} ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0100500 ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/1462 ! CAMK2D\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8158\" xsd:string\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8489\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1040014\nname: PPFIA3-related neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the PPFIA3 gene. This disorder is characterised by developmental delay and intellectual disability. Most patients present variable additional features, including dysmorphisms, microcephaly or macrocephaly, hypotonia, autism spectrum disorder or autistic features, abnormal electroencephalogram, and epilepsy.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, PMID:38181735]\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:621122\"}\nxref: OMIM:621122 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0100500 {source=\"PMID:38181735\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862\"} ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0100500 ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/9247 ! PPFIA3\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/9247 {source=\"OMIM:621122\"} ! PPFIA3\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8160\" xsd:string\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8489\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060117\nname: MYCBP2-related developmental delay with corpus callosum defects\ndef: \"Any neurodevelopmental disorder in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the MYCBP2 gene. This condition is characterized by variable corpus callosum defects consistent with dysgenesis, and a broad spectrum of neurobehavioural deficits including developmental delay, intellectual disability, epilepsy, and autistic features.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:36200388]\nsynonym: \"MDCD\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [PMID:36200388]\nsynonym: \"MYCBP2-related developmental delay with corpus callosum defects\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:36200388]\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"PMID:36200388\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700092 ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/23386 ! MYCBP2\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/23386 {source=\"PMID:36200388\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! MYCBP2\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9033\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060123\nname: GRIN1-related complex neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the GRIN1 gene. It is characterized by mild-to-profound developmental delay/intellectual disability (DD/ID) in all affected individuals. Other common manifestations are epilepsy, muscular hypotonia, movement disorders, spasticity, feeding difficulties, and behavior issues. A subset of individuals show a malformation of cortical development consisting of extensive and diffuse bilateral polymicrogyria.\" [PMID:31219694]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028154\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"GRIN1-related developmental and epileptic encephalopathy\" EXACT [PMID:31219694]\nsynonym: \"GRIN1-related neurodevelopmental disorder\" EXACT [PMID:31219694]\nxref: GARD:0028154 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"PMID:31219694\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nis_a: MONDO:1060138 {source=\"PMID:40374652\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! GRIN-related complex neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700092 ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/4584 ! GRIN1\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/4584 {source=\"PMID:31219694\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! GRIN1\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9063\" xsd:string\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060216\nname: TSEN2-related neurodevelopmental disorder with or without thrombotic microangiopathy\ndef: \"Any neurodevelopmental disorder in which the cause of the disease is a variation in the TSEN2 gene. This condition is associated with intellectual disability, growth delay, hypotonia, motor delay, ataxia, vision issues, cardiac features (including left ventricular hypertrophy), and pulmonary complications (such as acute respiratory distress and edema). It is also linked to brain structural anomalies such as pontine and cerebellar hypoplasia, cortical atrophy, and dilated ventricles. Renal features include proteinuria, thrombotic microangiopathy, end-stage kidney disease, and high-severity hypertension.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/, PMID:18711368, PMID:20952379, PMID:23562994, PMID:32404165, PMID:38347586, PMID:38438125, PMID:38622473]\nsynonym: \"TSEN2-related neurodevelopmental disorder with or without thrombotic microangiopathy\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/\"} ! syndromic disease\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700092 ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/28422 ! TSEN2\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/28422 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/\"} ! TSEN2\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9956\" xsd:anyURI\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
