{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"obo-grep.pl --noheader -r 'related neurodevelopmental disorder with' src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo\"","aggregated_output":"[Term]\nid: MONDO:0035706\nname: SETD2-related microcephaly-severe intellectual disability-multiple congenital anomalies syndrome\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0022397\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: nord_rare {source=\"MONDO:NORD\"}\nsubset: ordo_disorder {source=\"Orphanet:597743\"}\nsubset: orphanet {source=\"Orphanet:597743\"}\nsubset: orphanet_rare {source=\"Orphanet:597743\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: GARD:0022397 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:1843293 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: Orphanet:597743 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5681587 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:1843293\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153\"} ! syndromic disease\nis_a: MONDO:0800477 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/\"} ! SETD2-related neurodevelopmental disorder without or with macrocephaly/overgrowth\nrelationship: has_characteristic HP:0000006 {source=\"Orphanet:597743\"} ! Autosomal dominant inheritance\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/intellectual_developmental_disorder_autosomal_dominant_70\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/6599\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700281\nname: MYH10-related neurodevelopmental disorder with congenital anomalies\ndef: \"An autosomal dominant complex neurodevelopmental disorder in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the MYH10 gene.\" [PMID:25003005, PMID:35980381]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0027145\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: GARD:0027145 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0100465 {source=\"PMID:25003005\", source=\"PMID:35980381\"} ! complex neurodevelopmental disorder with or without congenital anomalies\nintersection_of: MONDO:0100038 ! complex neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_characteristic HP:0000006 ! Autosomal dominant inheritance\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/7568 ! MYH10\nrelationship: excluded_from_qc_check http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/sparql/qc/general/qc-single-child.sparql\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8100\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700358\nname: GABRA4-related neurodevelopmental disorder with seizures\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the GABRA4 gene. This disorder is characterised by developmental delay, epileptiform EEG abnormalities, and autism spectrum disorder, and/or attention deficit hyperactivity disorder. Other phenotypes observed less frequently include seizures, brain MRI abnormalities, and intellectual disability.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/ebi-gene2phenotype, PMID:38565639]\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"PMID:38565639\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/4078 {source=\"PMID:38565639\"} ! GABRA4\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9633\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700359\nname: GABRD-related neurodevelopmental disorder with epilepsy\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the GABRD gene. This disorder is characterised by developmental delay, generalized epilepsy with atypical absences and generalized myoclonic and/or bilateral tonic-clonic seizures, intellectual disability, and behavioural abnormalities.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/ebi-gene2phenotype, PMID:25156961, PMID:34633442]\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"PMID:25156961\", source=\"PMID:34633442\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/4084 {source=\"PMID:25156961\", source=\"PMID:34633442\"} ! GABRD\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9633\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700361\nname: RFX3-related neurodevelopmental disorder with autism and other behavioural abnormalities\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the RFX3 gene. This disorder is characterised by global developmental delay, intellectual disability, and behavioural abnormalities. Most patients present autism spectrum disorder and/or attention deficit hyperactivity disorder. Other phenotypes observed less frequently include sleep difficulties, micro or macrocephaly, non-specific and non-recurrent dysmorphisms, and brain MRI abnormalities.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/ebi-gene2phenotype, PMID:21792059, PMID:25844147, PMID:27525107, PMID:31981491, PMID:33658631, PMID:35982159, PMID:37717291]\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"PMID:21792059\", source=\"PMID:25844147\", source=\"PMID:27525107\", source=\"PMID:31981491\", source=\"PMID:33658631\", source=\"PMID:35982159\", source=\"PMID:37717291\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/9984 {source=\"PMID:21792059\", source=\"PMID:25844147\", source=\"PMID:27525107\", source=\"PMID:31981491\", source=\"PMID:33658631\", source=\"PMID:35982159\", source=\"PMID:37717291\"} ! RFX3\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9633\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700362\nname: RFX4-related neurodevelopmental disorder with autism and other behavioural abnormalities\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the RFX4 gene. This disorder is characterised by global developmental delay and/or intellectual disability, and behavioural abnormalities including documented autism spectrum disorder.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/ebi-gene2phenotype, PMID:25961944, PMID:33658631]\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"PMID:25961944\", source=\"PMID:33658631\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/9985 {source=\"PMID:25961944\", source=\"PMID:33658631\"} ! RFX4\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9633\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0800475\nname: NACC1-related neurodevelopmental disorder with epilepsy, cataracts and episodic irritability\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by heterozygous variants in NACC1 and characterized by developmental delay, intellectual disability, epilepsy, cataracts, feeding difficulties, and recurring episodes of extreme irritability. Other phenotypes include hypotonia, delayed myelination, microcephaly, stereotypic hand movements, gastrointestinal tract issues, and sleeping problems.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0027073\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"NACC1-related neurodevelopmental disorder with epilepsy, cataracts and episodic irritability\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0027073 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0001071 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/\"} ! intellectual disability\nis_a: MONDO:0100038 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/\"} ! complex neurodevelopmental disorder\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/20967 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/\"} ! NACC1\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/6700\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0800477\nname: SETD2-related neurodevelopmental disorder without or with macrocephaly/overgrowth\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by heterozygous variants in SETD2 and characterized by intellectual disability or developmental delay, motor delay, speech delay, hypotonia, autism spectrum disorder, attention deficit disorder, and sometimes features such as macrocephaly, overgrowth, and dysmorphic features.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/]\nsynonym: \"SETD2-related neurodevelopmental disorder without or with macrocephaly/overgrowth\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0001071 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/\"} ! intellectual disability\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/18420 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/\"} ! SETD2\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/6599\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0859190\nname: neurodevelopmental-craniofacial syndrome with variable renal and cardiac abnormalities\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:619522\"}\nsynonym: \"ZMYM2-related neurodevelopmental disorder with multiple anomalies\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163]\nxref: MEDGEN:1794194 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: OMIM:619522 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5561984 {source=\"MEDGEN:1794194\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0003847 {source=\"OMIM:619522\"} ! hereditary disease\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/12989 {source=\"OMIM:619522\"} ! ZMYM2\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/neurodevelopmental_craniofacial_syndrome_with_variable_renal_and_cardiac_abnormalities\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0859333\nname: intellectual developmental disorder, autosomal dominant 70\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0061043\"}\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:620157\"}\nxref: DOID:0061043 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:1824044 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: OMIM:620157 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5774271 {source=\"MEDGEN:1824044\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0100172 {source=\"OMIM:620157\"} ! intellectual disability, autosomal dominant\nis_a: MONDO:0800477 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/\"} ! SETD2-related neurodevelopmental disorder without or with macrocephaly/overgrowth\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/18420 {source=\"OMIM:620157\"} ! SETD2\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/6599\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1040003\nname: KCND2-related neurodevelopmental disorder with or without seizures\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the KCND2 gene. This disorder is characterized by early-onset global developmental delay with impaired motor, speech and cognitive development. Patients often present muscle hypotonia, and less frequently, developmental epileptic encephalopathy, visual impairment and physical dysmorphisms.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862, PMID:34245260]\nis_a: MONDO:0100500 {source=\"PMID:34245260\"} ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0987-9862\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700092 ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/6238 ! KCND2\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8155\" xsd:string\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8489\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060179\nname: RNU5B-1 related neurodevelopmental disorder with seizures and joint laxity\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder in which the cause of the disease is a variation in RNU5B-1 gene and is characterized by global developmental delay, hypotonia, macrocephaly, failure to thrive, abnormality of the eye, seizures, and joint laxity\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40060/, MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene, PMID:40379786, PMID:40442284]\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:621302\"}\nsynonym: \"NEDSJL\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [OMIM:621302]\nsynonym: \"neurodevelopmental disorder with seizures and joint laxity\" EXACT [OMIM:621302]\nsynonym: \"RNU5B-1 related neurodevelopmental disorder with seizures and joint laxity\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40060/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nsynonym: \"RNU5B-1-related disorder\" BROAD [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40060/]\nxref: OMIM:621302 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0100500 {source=\"PMID:40379786\", source=\"PMID:40442284\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40060/\"} ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0100500 ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/10212 ! RNU5B-1\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/10212 {source=\"OMIM:621302\", source=\"PMID:40379786\", source=\"PMID:40442284\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40060/\"} ! RNU5B-1\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator \"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\" xsd:string\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9596\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060216\nname: TSEN2-related neurodevelopmental disorder with or without thrombotic microangiopathy\ndef: \"Any neurodevelopmental disorder in which the cause of the disease is a variation in the TSEN2 gene. This condition is associated with intellectual disability, growth delay, hypotonia, motor delay, ataxia, vision issues, cardiac features (including left ventricular hypertrophy), and pulmonary complications (such as acute respiratory distress and edema). It is also linked to brain structural anomalies such as pontine and cerebellar hypoplasia, cortical atrophy, and dilated ventricles. Renal features include proteinuria, thrombotic microangiopathy, end-stage kidney disease, and high-severity hypertension.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/, PMID:18711368, PMID:20952379, PMID:23562994, PMID:32404165, PMID:38347586, PMID:38438125, PMID:38622473]\nsynonym: \"TSEN2-related neurodevelopmental disorder with or without thrombotic microangiopathy\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/\"} ! syndromic disease\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700092 ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/28422 ! TSEN2\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/28422 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/\"} ! TSEN2\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9956\" xsd:anyURI\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"compl