name: hemifacial microsomia, domestic cat\ndef: \"Any congenital malformation syndrome presenting with unilateral craniofacial abnormalities that occurs in cats.\" [PMID:22610383]\nsynonym: \"type III hemifacial microsomia, domestic cat\" RELATED [OMIA:001690-9685]\nxref: OMIA:001690-9685 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1011360 {source=\"OMIA:001690-9685\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! syndromic disease, non-human animal\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:9685 {source=\"OMIA:001690-9685\"} ! Felis catus\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7271\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1012754\nname: ptosis, intellectual disability, retarded growth and mortality syndrome, UBE3B-related, cattle\ndef: \"Any syndromic disease that occurs in cattle due to a mutation in the UBE3B gene.\" [MONDO:patterns/nonhuman_disease_series_by_gene]\nsynonym: \"PIRM\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [OMIA:001934-9913]\nsynonym: \"ptosis, intellectual disability, retarded growth and mortality (PIRM) syndrome (Haplotype AH1), cattle\" EXACT [OMIA:001934-9913]\nxref: OMIA:001934-9913 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1011321 {source=\"OMIA:001934-9913\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! hereditary disease, non-human animal\nis_a: MONDO:1011360 {source=\"OMIA:001934-9913\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! syndromic disease, non-human animal\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/ncbigene/512750 {source=\"OMIA:001934-9913\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! UBE3B\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:9913 {source=\"OMIA:001934-9913\"} ! Bos taurus\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7271\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1012860\nname: abnormal gait, retinal dysplasia, cataracts, RORB-related, rabbit\ndef: \"Abnormal locomotion defined by the loss of typical jumping and blindness at birth due to retinal dysplasia and early-onset cataracts that occurs in rabbits due to a mutation in the RORB gene.\" [PMID:33764968]\nxref: OMIA:002317-9986 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1011321 {source=\"OMIA:002317-9986\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! hereditary disease, non-human animal\nis_a: MONDO:1011360 {source=\"OMIA:002317-9986\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! syndromic disease, non-human animal\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/ncbigene/100345295 {source=\"OMIA:002317-9986\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! RORB\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:9986 {source=\"OMIA:002317-9986\"} ! Oryctolagus cuniculus\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7271\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1012887\nname: skeletal-cardio-enteric dysplasia, MAP2K2-related, cattle\ndef: \"Any syndromic congenital malformation characterized by reduced fetal growth, a short-spine, a long and narrow face, cardiac defects and heterotopy of the spiral colon that occurs in newborn cattle due to a mutation in the MAP2K2 gene.\" [PMID:34209498]\nsynonym: \"skeletal-cardio-enteric dysplasia\" RELATED [OMIA:002381-9913]\nxref: OMIA:002381-9913 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1011321 {source=\"OMIA:002381-9913\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! hereditary disease, non-human animal\nis_a: MONDO:1011360 {source=\"OMIA:002381-9913\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! syndromic disease, non-human animal\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/ncbigene/510434 {source=\"OMIA:002381-9913\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! MAP2K2\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:9913 {source=\"OMIA:002381-9913\"} ! Bos taurus\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7271\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1012909\nname: dental-skeletal-retinal anomaly, MIA3-related, dog\ndef: \"Brittle, discolored, translucent teeth, disproportionate growth and progressive retinal degeneration resulting in vision loss that occurs in dogs due to a mutation in the MIA3 gene.\" [PMID:34680893]\nxref: OMIA:002465-9615 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1011321 {source=\"OMIA:002465-9615\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! hereditary disease, non-human animal\nis_a: MONDO:1011360 {source=\"OMIA:002465-9615\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! syndromic disease, non-human animal\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/ncbigene/100855882 {source=\"OMIA:002465-9615\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! MIA3\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:9615 {source=\"OMIA:002465-9615\"} ! Canis lupus familiaris\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7271\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1012939\nname: perinatal mortality syndrome, GCK-related, cattle\ndef: \"Any syndromic disease characterized by perinatal mortality that occurs in cattle due to a mutation in the GCK gene.\" [MONDO:patterns/nonhuman_disease_series_by_gene]\nxref: OMIA:002579-9913 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1011321 {source=\"OMIA:002579-9913\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! hereditary disease, non-human animal\nis_a: MONDO:1011360 {source=\"OMIA:002579-9913\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! syndromic disease, non-human animal\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/ncbigene/616576 {source=\"OMIA:002579-9913\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! GCK\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:9913 {source=\"OMIA:002579-9913\"} ! Bos taurus\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7271\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1040010\nname: IRF6-related condition\ndef: \"Van der Woude syndrome, popliteal pterygium syndrome, cleft lip with or without palate, or a spectrum of one or two of those conditions in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the IRF6 gene.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40059/, PMID:12219090, PMID:20301581]\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"PMID:12219090\", source=\"PMID:20301581\"} ! syndromic disease\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date \"2024-07-12T13:35:21Z\" xsd:dateTime\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7493\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1040022\nname: linkeropathy\ndef: \"Group of rare heritable connective tissue disorders, characterized by a variable degree of short stature, skeletal dysplasia, joint laxity, cutaneous anomalies, dysmorphism, heart malformation, and developmental delay. The LK genes encode for enzymes that add glycosaminoglycan chains onto proteoglycans via a common tetrasaccharide linker region.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5493-2602, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693, PMID:31196143, PMID:31438591, PMID:37657630]\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"PMID:31196143\", source=\"PMID:31438591\", source=\"PMID:37657630\"} ! syndromic disease\nis_a: MONDO:0003900 {source=\"PMID:31196143\", source=\"PMID:31438591\"} ! connective tissue disorder\nis_a: MONDO:0005516 {source=\"PMID:31438591\", source=\"PMID:37657630\"} ! osteochondrodysplasia\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8179\" xsd:string\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1040023\nname: NDUFB11-related disorders\ndef: \"A group of rare genetic conditions caused by variants in the NDUFB11 gene. Presentation is heterogenous including neurologic, cardiac, ocular, and dermatological abnormalities.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693, https://orcid.org/0000-001-9310-0163, PMID:25772934, PMID:25921236, PMID:26741492, PMID:27102574]\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"PMID:25772934\", source=\"PMID:27102574\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\"} ! syndromic disease\nintersection_of: MONDO:0002254 ! syndromic disease\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/20372 ! NDUFB11\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8253\" xsd:string\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060150\nname: NOTCH1-related AOS spectrum disorder\ndef: \"A disease characterized by a spectrum of cardiac and extracardiac phenotypes caused by a disease-causing variant in the NOTCH1 gene, inherited in an autosomal dominant manner. Affected individuals may present with congenital heart defects, bicuspid aortic valve, aortic valve stenosis, thoracic aortic aneurysm or dissection, anomalies in brain structure, intracranial or posterior circulation vascular anomalies, cutaneous vascular malformations, cutis marmorata, and/or a phenotype compatible with Adams-Oliver syndrome (i.e. cutis aplasia, terminal limb defects, skull ossification defects).\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40104/, https://orcid.org/0009-0007-6180-2639, PMID:25963545]\ncomment: Variants in NOTCH1 have been reported in individuals with the following disease entities: Adams-Oliver Syndrome, congenital heart disease, aortic valve disease including bicuspid aortic valve, and thoracic aortic aneurysm and dissection. Individuals with pathogenic variants in NOTCH1 may also be asymptomatic due to incomplete penetrance and extensive intrafamilial variability. Per criteria outlined by the ClinGen Lumping and Splitting guidelines, we found no difference in molecular mechanism and inheritance pattern and found considerable interfamilial and intrafamilial variability in cardiac phenotypes. Therefore, Adams-Oliver syndrome 5 and aortic valve disease 1 have been lumped into one disease entity (NOTCH1-related AOS spectrum disorder).\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"PMID:25963545\", source=\"PMID:38778082\"} ! syndromic disease\nis_a: MONDO:0005453 {source=\"PMID:38778082\", source=\"PMID:40127276\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40104/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0009-0007-6180-2639\"} ! congenital heart disease\nrelationship: has_characteristic HP:0000006 {source=\"PMID:25963545\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40104/\"} ! Autosomal dominant inheritance\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/7881 {source=\"PMID:25963545\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40104/\"} ! NOTCH1\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9236\" xsd:string\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9832\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060192\nname: CASK-related intellectual disability\ndef: \"A syndromic disorder in which the cause of the disease is a variation in the CASK gene. It is associated with a wide phenotypic spectrum ranging from mild-to-severe intellectual disability with or without nystagmus to moderate-to-profound intellectual disability and progressive microcephaly with pontine and cerebellar hypoplasia, often associated with seizures.\" [MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene, PMID:24278995]\nsynonym: \"CASK-related disorder\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:24278995]\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"PMID:24278995\"} ! syndromic disease\nis_a: MONDO:0020119 {source=\"PMID:24278995\"} ! X-linked syndromic intellectual disability\nintersection_of: MONDO:0000508 ! syndromic intellectual disability\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/1497 ! CASK\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9747\" xsd:string\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060197\nname: congenital heart disease with heterotaxy syndrome\ndef: \"A heart disease that is present at birth that occurs with variable extracardiac laterality defects. Features of visceral heterotaxy are not always present but can include abnormal location of the organs within the thoracic, abdominal, or peritoneal cavities. Anatomic and functional problems can include intestinal malrotation leading to volvulus, biliary atresia, and various defects of the central nervous system, urinary tract, and skeleton.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40130/, PMID:19064609, PMID:30293987, PMID:34666056]\nsynonym: \"congenital heart disease with heterotaxy syndrome\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40130/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40130/\"} ! syndromic disease\nis_a: MONDO:0005453 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40130/\"} ! congenital heart disease\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9463\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060212\nname: CRYAB-related myofibrillar myopathy-cataract-cardiomyopathy spectrum disorder\ndef: \"A syndromic disease caused by a variation in the CRYAB gene, and characterized by a spectrum of phenotypes including cardiomyopathy, cataract, and/or myopathy.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280, PMID:21920752, PMID:38212463]\nsynonym: \"alpha-B crystallinopathy\" RELATED [PMID:21920752]\nsynonym: \"CRYAB-related myofibrillar myopathy-cataract-cardiomyopathy spectrum disorder\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280\"} ! syndromic disease\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/2389 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280\"} ! CRYAB\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9774\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060216\nname: TSEN2-related neurodevelopmental disorder with or without thrombotic microangiopathy\ndef: \"Any neurodevelopmental disorder in which the cause of the disease is a variation in the TSEN2 gene. This condition is associated with intellectual disability, growth delay, hypotonia, motor delay, ataxia, vision issues, cardiac features (including left ventricular hypertrophy), and pulmonary complications (such as acute respiratory distress and edema). It is also linked to brain structural anomalies such as pontine and cerebellar hypoplasia, cortical atrophy, and dilated ventricles. Renal features include proteinuria, thrombotic microangiopathy, end-stage kidney disease, and high-severity hypertension.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/, PMID:18711368, PMID:20952379, PMID:23562994, PMID:32404165, PMID:38347586, PMID:38438125, PMID:38622473]\nsynonym: \"TSEN2-related neurodevelopmental disorder with or without thrombotic microangiopathy\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/\"} ! syndromic disease\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700092 ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/28422 ! TSEN2\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/28422 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/\"} ! TSEN2\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9956\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770554\nname: peracute mortality syndrome, red panda\nxref: OMIA:002911-9649 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1011360 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! syndromic disease, non-human animal\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:9649 {source=\"OMIA:002911-9649\"} ! Ailurus fulgens\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/10159\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:8000010\nname: antiphospholipid syndrome\ndef: \"A disorder caused by the presence of autoantibodies directed against phospholipids, causing a hypercoaguable state, which may result in blood clots, stroke, heart attack, and in women, significant pregnancy-related complications, including miscarriage and still birth. The syndrome is often associated with other autoimmune disorders, most commonly lupus erythematosus, and infections, including syphilis and Lyme disease.\" [NCIT:C61283]\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:2988\"}\nsubset: doid_rare {source=\"DOID:2988\"}\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0005824\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: ncit {source=\"NCIT:C61283\"}\nsubset: ordo_disorder {source=\"Orphanet:80\"}\nsubset: orphanet {source=\"Orphanet:80\"}\nsubset: orphanet_rare {source=\"Orphanet:80\"}\nsubset: otar {source=\"MONDO:OTAR\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"antiphospholipid antibody syndrome\" EXACT [DOID:2988, ICD10CM:D68.61, NCIT:C61283, Orphanet:80]\nsynonym: \"antiphospholipid syndrome\" EXACT [DOID